            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "My preference is that we consider this document deprecated. I think it represents a good set of suggestions for mapping of net names to behaviours *in userspace*. Devicetrees represent the hardware, and from experience over time I think it's best that they reflect the information from the schematics without influence from software implementation choices."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Derek Howard",
                        "email": "derekh@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "derekhoward55"
                    },
                    "message": "That's fine with me, will let Patrick and/or Andrew weigh in."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "I think this document and the proposals in it have been more work then they were really worth and there was a lot of friction with userspace dictating kernel device tree rules.\n\nBut I'm not sure a comment on a review just trying to update it is the place to make a decision to deprecate it? A mailing list or TOF issue maybe? I think in the end we need to guide people towards using a standard name if possible but also encouraging openbmc userspace apps to support build-time configuration data to allow whatever the device tree for a system serves up."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "> A mailing list or TOF issue maybe?\n\nI've started a thread on the mailing list:\n\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/all/eff663ee55f2614dde750f5f0669ec876f107c0d.camel@codeconstruct.com.au/"
                }
            ],
